Merge two KG nodes of the same node_type. The fold_id node is folded
into keep_id: every edge pointing at fold_id gets rewritten to point at
keep_id, the fold node's label + aliases are added to keep's aliases,
and the fold node is deleted. Atomic. Reversible via the kg_revision_log
entry. Refuses to merge across different node_types.

Use for the duplicate / typo-variant case (e.g. "Aleks" should be
merged into "Alex"). Always pass a non-empty `reason`. Pass
`dry_run: true` to see the diff without committing.
